comments.message:
So it looks like we're working with a `struct pldm_state_sensor_pdr`. In which case, we should do:

```
LIBPLDM_NONNULL
static int decode_pldm_state_sensor_pdr(...)
{
    /* The usual msgbuf extraction stuff */
    ...
}

LIBPLDM_ABI_TESTING
int pldm_pdr_delete_by_sensor_id(...)
{
    ...


    struct pldm_state_sensor_pdr pdr;
    int rc;

    if (!record->data) {
        return -ENOENT;
    }

    rc = decode_pldm_state_sensor_pdr(record->data, record->size, &pdr);
    if (rc) {
        return rc;
    }

    if (record->is_remote != is_remote || pdr.hdr_type != PLDM_STATE_SENSOR_PDR) {
        goto cleanup;
    }

    ...
```

All this opaque skipping is not maintainable.
